<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · ideology</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pacifism</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1815 CE – present</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pacifism is the opposition to war or violence, from the belief that disputes can be settled peacefully to the rejection of all force. It has ancient precedents, took organised form in the peace movements of 1815 and 1816, and was named in 1901.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Nehru's two biggest failures are thought to be the partition of India and the Sino-Indian War of 1962, in which his policy is said to have been influenced by Gandhian <b>pacifism</b>.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/gandhism">Gandhism · In Power</a></li></ul></section>
